#!/usr/bin/env node
// Generates the originals for the dashboard's "See it work" demos through a running Crackio
// (pnpm dev) and the plans you've connected. Every take lands full size in assets-src/showcase
// (gitignored); the demos use finished copies in public/assets/showcase/<demo>/.
//
// Images are Grok Imagine 2.0 (several takes; the one kept is the parent of what follows, named
// "<id>-<take>"). Edits are ChatGPT Images, which keep everything they weren't asked to change
// within a pixel or two, so before/after frames line up. Clips are Grok Imagine Video 1.5.
//
// The takes the demos use: image-takes-4 (Image), video-still-4, retouch-base-1, relight-portrait-2,
// product-pack-2, cast-a-2, motion-boat-2 and -3, motion-product-2, recast-src-3, story-door-2,
// upscale-eye-1, car-2, billboard-2. Director's three photographs are staged first: clay-*.png are
// frames of its three.js set (window.__clay in dev), and each shot is the clay frame turned into a
// photograph of the woman in woman-ref.png.
//
// The third cut adds: w-* (Image's other 43 worlds, Grok edits of image-takes-4), up-wide-4 and
// its two enhances up-l1-g1 and up-l2-c (Upscale), dir-woman-1 and one take each of the props and
// backdrops (Director), m-* stills and mv-* clips (Motion), pv-* clips (Product), render-1-c and
// render-2-c and their -life clips (Director). A few steps happen in between, by hand:
//   - Cut-outs and masks come from Crackio's vision model (POST /api/vision {task: "cutout" | "mask"}):
//     dir-*-cut.png, car-frames/*.png (car-frames-raw: 17 stills of car-orbit-a and -b, cut out) and
//     masks/image/<world>.png (her silhouette in each world, for the alignment).
//   - guide-1.png and guide-2.png are frames of Director's three.js set at its two renders
//     (window.__stage in dev, at the times in window.__renders); render-n.png is render-n-c
//     aligned to its guide (ECC), the start frame of render-n-life.
//   - pd-<scene>-al.png (Product's stills locked on the bottle, the start frames of pv-*) come from
//     showcase-finish.py product_stills.
//
// Then scripts/assets/showcase-finish.py lines everything up and writes public/assets/showcase/:
// the variants are aligned to their original (OpenCV ECC), Retouch's colorways only change the bag
// and the sweater, Cast's places are aligned on her eyes, and the clips are cut and re-encoded.
// Depth maps (depth/*.png) come from Crackio's own depth model (POST /api/vision {task: "depth"}).
//
// Usage: node scripts/assets/showcase.mjs [id ...]      (needs Crackio on http://127.0.0.1:3210)
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import path from "node:path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";
import { spawnSync } from "node:child_process";
import { createRequire } from "node:module";
import sharp from "sharp";

const here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
const root = path.resolve(here, "../..");
const BASE = process.env.CRACKIO_URL ?? "http://127.0.0.1:3210";
const IMAGE = "grok:grok-imagine-image-2.0";
const outDir = path.join(root, "assets-src", "showcase");

/**
 * parent: the take this one edits or animates ("frame:<clip>@<seconds|end>" is a still from a clip);
 * parents: several references, each with its role; video: seconds; recast: a Grok video edit of
 * the parent clip.
 */
